###Mapping
// The trade-surveillance mapping.
//
// Every set id is named EXPLICITLY and sur-prefixed. That is not decoration: set ids are a
// GLOBAL namespace in Legend, and SurCaseRelation has trade_surveillance::SurCase on BOTH
// of its ends, so each of its two association ends has to name a source AND a target set --
// [surCase, surCase], the same id twice, in both directions. Only the direction of travel
// over @Sur_RelatedCase distinguishes `relatedCase` from `linkedCases`.
//
// Because every set here is explicit, `trade_surveillance_SurAlert` and its siblings do NOT
// exist. Anything downstream must name the `sur` ids.
//
// The two upstream mappings are included so the cross-project association ends can name
// their far set ids. Those ids come from the dependencies' MANIFESTs rather than from a
// guess: order-execution names all of its sets explicitly, so `oexFill`,
// `oexOrderFillSummary` and `oexTradeBooking` are the ids and `order_execution_Fill` does
// not exist; trade-lifecycle's amendment set is `tlcAmendment`. The two closures overlap on
// trade-capture and the diamond closes.
//
// The eleven EnumerationMappings are the only place the physical code strings live. Each
// accepts a short code and the spelled-out form, because the vendor surveillance platform
// emits the short code and the case-management system emits the long one.
Mapping trade_surveillance::Mapping
(
   include order_execution::Mapping
   include trade_lifecycle::Mapping

   // ---- Enumeration mappings ----

   trade_surveillance::SurAlertType: EnumerationMapping SurAlertTypeMapping
   {
      SPOOFING:                  ['SPOOF', 'SPOOFING'],
      LAYERING:                  ['LAYER', 'LAYERING'],
      WASH_TRADE:                ['WASH', 'WASH_TRADE'],
      MARKING_THE_CLOSE:         ['MKCLS', 'MARKING_THE_CLOSE'],
      MOMENTUM_IGNITION:         ['MOMIG', 'MOMENTUM_IGNITION'],
      FRONT_RUNNING:             ['FRUN', 'FRONT_RUNNING'],
      INSIDER_DEALING:           ['INSDR', 'INSIDER_DEALING'],
      QUOTE_STUFFING:            ['QSTUF', 'QUOTE_STUFFING'],
      RAMPING:                   ['RAMP', 'RAMPING'],
      CROSS_MARKET_MANIPULATION: ['XMKT', 'CROSS_MARKET_MANIPULATION'],
      AMENDMENT_PATTERN:         ['AMDPT', 'AMENDMENT_PATTERN'],
      UNAUTHORISED_TRADING:      ['UNAUT', 'UNAUTHORISED_TRADING']
   }

   trade_surveillance::SurAlertStatus: EnumerationMapping SurAlertStatusMapping
   {
      NEW:                 ['NEW', 'NEW'],
